# Stay inside the repo

This is a work machine. Nothing for AmbientMind may be written outside
`~/AmbientMind`: no global installs, caches, app data, keychain items, login
items, global git/npm/Cursor config, or models in `~/.ollama`.

- Run every Node/npm/Electron/Swift command through the wrapper:
  `./dev npm run dev`, `./dev npm test`, `./dev run <cmd>`. Never bare `npm`,
  `npx`, `node`, `electron`, `swift`, `brew`, `pip`.
- First-time setup is `./dev setup` (pinned Node from `.node-version` into
  `.local/node`, then `npm ci` with caches in `.local/cache`).
- Ollama: `./dev ollama start` runs a project instance on port 11435 with models
  in `.local/ollama/models`. Never use `ollama pull` against the global server.
- Packaged builds: launch only with `./dev packaged`, never by double-clicking.
- MCP servers, skills and rules go in this repo's `.cursor/` only, never in
  `~/.cursor`. Give MCP servers `npm_config_cache` pointing into `.local/cache`.
- Scratch files, downloads, screenshots and reference clones go in `.local/`,
  never `/tmp`.
- Git identity is repo-local; don't touch `git config --global`.
- After running the app, `./dev doctor` must report nothing outside the repo;
  `./dev clean-system` removes the traces macOS keeps for apps that ran.
